    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^x=e^{x\\ln a}$ for $a>0$.\n\nUse $e^{\\ln a}=a$ and the index power law.",
      "worked": "For $a>0$, use $e^{\\ln a}=a$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}e^{x\\ln a}&=\\big(e^{\\ln a}\\big)^x\\\\e^{x\\ln a}&=a^x.\\end{align*}$$",
